      {
        "text": "And it came to pass as timber was exceedingly scarce in the land northward, they did send forth much by the way of shipping.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 115,
            "end": 123,
            "text": "Alma 63:7 (5–8)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 10,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 3:10",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And thus they did enable the people in the land northward that they might build many cities, both of wood and of cement.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 3:11",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass that there were many of the people of Ammon, who were Lamanites by birth, did also go forth into this land.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 48,
            "end": 54,
            "text": "Alma 27:26; 63:9 (4–9); Hel. 6:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Helaman 3:12",
        "book": "Helaman",
        "chapter": 3,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And now there are many records kept of the proceedings of this people, by many of this people, which are particular and very large, concerning them.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 23,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "W of M 1:3 (1–11)."
